ooRexx (third_party/ooRexx, a pinned unmodified submodule) is not part of this
repository's source, and built binaries contain none of its code. Its
interpreter is the reference the tests compare against. A regular build does
not read the submodule. interrexx-classes and interrexx-inventory build from
checked-in tables of interface facts (class and method names, arities, error
numbers and the names of the built-in functions), which `interrexx-upstream`
derived from Setup.cpp, BuiltinFunctions.cpp and rexxmsg.xml when the pinned
revision changed. The directive options table of the extracted documentation
derives from DirectiveParser.cpp. The texts of the error messages are
interrexx's own.

ooTest and the ooRexx documentation are fetched by scripts/setup-third-party.sh
and are not redistributed here.
